    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The future with «werden + Infinitiv»",
     "texto": [
      "Although the present is often used for everyday plans, the formal future tense (*Futur I*) is formed with the auxiliary **werden**:",
      "1. **Conjugation of «werden»:**",
      "**ich werde, du wirst, er/sie/es wird, wir werden, ihr werdet, sie/Sie werden**.",
      "2. **Verb bracket structure:**",
      "The auxiliary *werden* takes the **second position** and the main verb in the infinitive goes to the **very end** of the sentence:",
      "**Morgen werde ich meine Freunde besuchen.** (Tomorrow I will visit my friends).",
      "**Im Sommer werden wir nach Berlin reisen.** (In summer we will travel to Berlin).",
      "3. **Questions about plans:**",
      "**Was wirst du am Wochenende machen?** (What will you do at the weekend?).",
      "**Wirst du morgen Zeit haben?** (Will you have time tomorrow?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
